etude. Escrever no pipe não prova que o fornecedor consumiu o prompt. Sessões e chaves privadas ficam fora da prova pública.\n \n-Visualize `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <nome> [--ttl <duração>]` e acrescente `--apply` para publicar uma prova imutável em `.pose/review-run-proofs/`. TTL é opcional (sem expiração quando ausente), positivo quando informado e limitado a 365 dias. Verifique com `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. A prova assina a declaração capturada do executor; não é recibo independente do fornecedor nem confirmação humana. Auditorias failed/interrupted mostram seu estado e `complete_review=false`. Decisão desconhecida ou ambígua também mantém a flag falsa. A flag verdadeira descreve entrega concluída com uma decisão de draft, não aprovação nem validação completa da conclusão tipada. Run completed com stdin incompleto ou saída truncada não estabelece review concluído. Runs legados sem proveniência capturada não são promovidos assinando a configuração atual.\n+Visualize `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <nome> [--ttl <duração>]` e acrescente `--apply` para publicar uma prova imutável em `.pose/review-run-proofs/`. TTL é opcional (sem expiração quando ausente), positivo quando informado e limitado a 365 dias. Verifique com `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. A prova assina a declaração capturada do executor; não é recibo independente do fornecedor nem confirmação humana. Auditorias failed/interrupted mostram seu estado e `complete_review=false`. Decisão desconhecida ou ambígua também mantém a flag falsa. A flag verdadeira descreve entrega concluída com uma decisão de draft, não aprovação nem validação completa da conclusão tipada. Run completed com stdin incompleto ou saída truncada não estabelece review concluído. Runs legados sem proveniência capturada não são promovidos assinando a configuração atual. `pose review run-proof` e os demais leitores do veredito de uma run fazem a pergunta que o fechamento faz: para uma run cujo escopo está done, a prova como foi dada (o registro se sustenta, o emissor mantém o pin; a deriva rotineira do repositório e a expiração da prova não são perguntadas, porque a expiração limita quando uma prova pode amparar uma nova atestação, não se uma atestação já dada a um escopo done se mantém); para um escopo aberto, como o repositório está agora.\n \n Acrescente `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` a uma solicitação completa de `pose review attest`. O issuer deriva do run os vínculos de principal/execução e assina a referência exata. Critérios, tools, evidências e preflight continuam obrigatórios. Draft negativo ou ambíguo não apoia aprovação; a atestação não pode anteceder o término do run ou sua prova assinada. Provas de adjudication/smoke vinculam seus kinds e não servem como atestações de review. Validar/aplicar automaticamente conclusões completas e tipadas pertence à capability, não à assinatura do run.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go\nindex 31f899c1..ba4b7074 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_provenance.go\n@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ func cmdReviewRunProof(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int\n \tif len(args) < 2 || len(args) > 3 || len(args) == 3 && args[2] != \"--json\" {\n \t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"Usage: pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]\")\n \t}\n-\tproof, e := cliGovernedStore(root).VerifyReviewRunProof(args[0], args[1])\n+\tproof, e := cliGovernedStore(root).VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(args[0], args[1])\n \tif e != nil {\n \t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review run proof: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(e.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n \t\treturn 1\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\nindex 92db118f..be17f39d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go\n@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ func (s Store) verifiedVerdictOf(kind, runID string) (*verifiedVerdict, string)\n \t\treturn nil, \"the run's draft cannot be read\"\n \t}\n \tissuer := \"\"\n-\tif assurance, err := s.VerifyReviewRunProof(runID, proof); err == nil {\n+\tif assurance, err := s.VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(runID, proof); err == nil {\n \t\tissuer = assurance.Issuer\n \t}\n \treturn &verifiedVerdict{ProofID: proof, Issuer: issuer, BundleID: run.BundleID, Scope: run.Scope, Decision: draft.Decision}, \"\"\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go\nindex 488bb2b6..8d5f7452 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go\n@@ -137,3 +137,50 @@ func TestTheAssuranceOfARetainedDelegatedApprovalIsVerified(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the assurance of a retained delegated approval is not the sealed run's: %+v\", assurance)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Spec pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question, R1 and R3: after routine drift of a done\n+// scope the closeout keeps the approval, and the reader of the run's proof answers as the\n+// closeout does, where the live verifier refuses.\n+func TestTheProofReaderAndTheCloseoutAgreeOnADoneScopeWithDrift(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf, run := approvedByARunThenDone(t)\n+\tcommitReviewFixture(t, f.store.Root, \"false\")\n+\tif verification, err := f.store.VerifyReviewBundle(f.bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref); err != nil || !verification.Approved {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the closeout must keep the approval, or this test proves nothing: %+v %v\", verification.Blockers, err)\n+\t}\n+\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(f.store.Root, filepath.FromSlash(reviewRunProofDir), run.RunID))\n+\tif err != nil || len(entries) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run's proof: %v %v\", entries, err)\n+\t}\n+\tproofID := strings.TrimSuffix(entries[0].Name(), \".json\")\n+\tif _, err := f.store.VerifyReviewRunProof(run.RunID, proofID); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the live verifier accepted a run whose scope drifted: the fixture shows no disagreement\")\n+\t}\n+\tif assurance, err := f.store.VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(run.RunID, proofID); err != nil || !assurance.CompleteReview {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the reader disagrees with the closeout about a done scope: %+v %v\", assurance, err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R3 (open scope): the reader keeps the live question while the scope is open.\n+func TestTheProofReaderKeepsTheLiveQuestionForAnOpenScope(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf, draftPath := conclusionFixture(t)\n+\tatt := approvedBundleAttestation(f.bundle, \"agent:reviewer\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(draftPath, []byte(draftFrom(t, att, nil)), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun := dispatchConclusion(t, f, \"an open scope\")\n+\tif _, err := f.store.ConcludeReviewRun(run.RunID, f.key.Name, true, time.Now()); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, kv := range [][]string{{\"user.name\", \"fixture\"}, {\"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"}, {\"commit.gpgsign\", \"false\"}} {\n+\t\tfederatedTestGit(t, f.store.Root, \"config\", kv[0], kv[1])\n+\t}\n+\tcommitReviewFixture(t, f.store.Root, \"false\")\n+\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(f.store.Root, filepath.FromSlash(reviewRunProofDir), run.RunID))\n+\tif err != nil || len(entries) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run's proof: %v %v\", entries, err)\n+\t}\n+\tproofID := strings.TrimSuffix(entries[0].Name(), \".json\")\n+\tif _, err := f.store.VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(run.RunID, proofID); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"an open scope was read as sealed\")\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\nindex 901542bd..b660055d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\n@@ -507,7 +507,7 @@ func (s Store) recoveredReviewConclusion(pending ReviewConclusion) (*ReviewConcl\n \t\tdone.State, done.Attestation, done.ProofID, done.BundleID, done.Scope, done.Decision, done.Destination = ReviewConclusionRecorded, att.AttestationID, att.Run.ProofID, att.BundleID, bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref, att.Decision, \"\"\n \t\t// The issuer is the one that signed the run's proof, never the\n \t\t// reservation's (review round 2, R2-F02).\n-\t\tif assurance, err := s.VerifyReviewRunProof(att.Run.RunID, att.Run.ProofID); err == nil {\n+\t\tif assurance, err := s.VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(att.Run.RunID, att.Run.ProofID); err == nil {\n \t\t\tdone.Issuer = assurance.Issuer\n \t\t}\n \t\tdone.Reasons = []string{\"completed from the attestation an interrupted conclusion recorded\"}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\nindex 39fea5b7..5335a711 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\n@@ -659,6 +659,24 @@ func (s Store) runApprovalAsSealed(bundle ReviewBundle) bool {\n \treturn err == nil && done\n }\n \n+// VerifyReviewRunProofForReading verifies a signed run proof for a reader that reports on a\n+// run: as it was given when the scope the run reviewed is done, as it is now otherwise. It is\n+// the question the closeout asks (verifyRunReviewReference), so a reader and the closeout\n+// cannot disagree about one run (spec pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question). On the\n+// sealed path the expiry of the proof is not asked: it bounds the window in which a proof may\n+// back a new attestation, and an attestation already given to a done scope stands.\n+func (s Store) VerifyReviewRunProofForReading(id, proofID string) (ReviewRunAssurance, error) {\n+\ts = s.reviewOperation()\n+\trun, e := s.LoadProvenanceReviewRun(id)\n+\tif e != nil {\n+\t\treturn ReviewRunAssurance{}, e\n+\t}\n+\tif bundle, e := s.LoadReviewBundle(run.BundleID); e == nil && s.runApprovalAsSealed(bundle) {\n+\t\treturn s.VerifyReviewRunProofAsSealed(id, proofID)\n+\t}\n+\treturn s.VerifyReviewRunProof(id, proofID)\n+}\n+\n func validProofDigest(value string) bool {\n \treturn regexp.MustCompile(`^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$`).MatchString(value)\n }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md b/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\nindex 1c94ad60..552f131a 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n@@ -1047,7 +1047,7 @@ Declare the executor and implementation baseline before dispatch. A bundle that\n \n Use the existing native issuer and its attestation pin. Set protected `authority_project` and `authority_audience` in review policy; a declared project identity must agree. Keep keys outside the project. Dispatch captures origin/worktree, bundle/commit/scope/kind, configuration/argv/executable, identities, brief template/body/notes, planned stdin and actual pipe-write digests, raw and retained redacted output/transcript digests and completeness. A pipe write does not prove the vendor consumed the prompt. Session references and private keys stay outside the public proof.\n \n-Preview `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>]`, then add `--apply` to publish an immutable proof under `.pose/review-run-proofs/`. TTL is optional (no expiry when absent), positive when supplied and at most 365 days. Verify it with `pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]`. The proof signs the captured executor declaration; it is not an independent vendor receipt or human confirmation. Failed or interrupted audit records disclose their state and `complete_review=false`. Unknown or ambiguous draft decisions also keep that flag false. A true flag describes completed delivery with one draft decision, not approval or complete typed-conclusion validation. A completed run with incomplete stdin or truncated output cannot establish a completed review. Legacy runs have no captured p